assumptions='For EVERY positive prefix n<=T, supplied leader n lies in V and minimizes the prefix sum against EVERY u in V. Both membership and prefix argmin are premises; minimizer existence is not constructed. For T>0 this data implies V inhabited; T0 is a vacuous empty-sum extension with no condition on leader0.'
information='The auxiliary hindsight leader at prefix n includes the current loss. It is NOT the causal FTL prediction, which uses the strict past. Lemma1.2 alone produces no learner, no-regret/logarithmic rate, stochastic expectation or minimax theorem. Teaching links to those later results are not actual proof dependencies of this lemma.'
index='Source loss ell_(t+1) is Lean loss t; source x*_n is leader n. Lean diagonal uses leader(t+1) over rangeT; the fixed comparison uses leaderT. T1 has identical sides. Existing induction cancels the final summand, applies the previous prefix inequality, then uses prefix argmin with the feasible next/final leader.'
tests='Actual changing Bool canary: false always costs0, true costs-2 then3, feasible prefix leaders true thenfalse. It produces all prefix argmins and proves diagonal-2 versus final0, hence STRICT -2<0. Keeping feasible leaders false thentrue violates prefix optimality (-2<0 at prefix1) and reverses comparison3>1. Separately, ambient losses true:-10 then5 / false:0 with V={false} and leaders false thentrue satisfy ALL prefix comparisons against V, but finalleader lies outside V and reverse comparison5>-5. This is an ambient-extension test showing the necessity of feasibility, not an admissible trajectory for a source loss defined only on V. Empty/one-horizon boundary tests are separate named proofs.'
